# loop-supervisor loads this file (as .env, via python-dotenv) before
# starting `opencode serve`, so any credential your provider needs must
# be set here rather than assumed to already be in your shell.
#
# This project's opencode.json ships with no provider configured (see
# docs/decisions/ in the loop-supervisor project this depends on for why)
# -- add your own provider block there, referencing whatever environment
# variable names you choose with OpenCode's `{env:VAR_NAME}` syntax, then
# list those same names below with their real values.
#
# Example, if you configure an OpenAI-compatible provider named "my-provider":
#   MY_PROVIDER_API_KEY=
